(- Redis for counters, lockout keys, and cache.) Tj
T*
(- Kafka topics for asynchronous event publication.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. MAJOR BUILDING BLOCKS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `RateLimitFilter`: computes caller identity, evaluates quota decision, returns 429 when) Tj
T*
(required.) Tj
T*
(- `RateLimitService`: rule resolution and algorithm dispatch.) Tj
T*
(- `RateLimitAlgorithmFactory`: runtime strategy selection.) Tj
T*
(- `SlidingWindowAlgorithm`, `TokenBucketAlgorithm`, `FixedWindowAlgorithm`: Redis-backed) Tj
T*
(controls.) Tj
T*
(- `JWTAuthFilter` and `JWTTokenProvider`: token validation and identity propagation.) Tj
T*
(- `OTPService`: OTP generation/verification and lockout handling.) Tj
T*
(- `PaymentService`: idempotency guard \(Redis + MySQL\) and payment lifecycle transitions.) Tj
T*
(- `NotificationDispatcherService`: non-blocking event publishing to Kafka topics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. KEY RUNTIME FLOWS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.1 REQUEST RATE-LIMIT ENFORCEMENT) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Request enters filter chain.) Tj
T*
(2. `JWTAuthFilter` validates token \(if present\) and sets `clientId` request attribute.) Tj
T*
(3. `RateLimitFilter` resolves effective `clientId` and route.) Tj
T*
(4. `RateLimitService` resolves applicable rule \(exact > wildcard > global > fallback\).) Tj
T*
(5. Selected algorithm checks allowance in Redis.) Tj
T*
(6. Response headers are set \(`X-RateLimit-*`\).) Tj
T*
(7. If denied, HTTP 429 is returned; otherwise request continues to controller.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.2 OTP FLOW) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Client calls generate endpoint.) Tj
T*
(2. Service verifies lock status in Redis.) Tj
T*
(3. OTP is generated, hashed, persisted, and dispatched as notification event.) Tj
T*
(4. Verify endpoint checks latest active OTP, expiry, attempts, and hash match.) Tj
T*
(5. On excessive failures, lock key is set in Redis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.3 PAYMENT FLOW) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Client submits payment with `Idempotency-Key`.) Tj
T*
(2. Redis short-circuit check runs first; MySQL check is fallback durability layer.) Tj
T*
(3. For new key, payment is created and processed.) Tj
T*
(4. Payment status transitions to SUCCESS/FAILED and is persisted.) Tj
T*
(5. Notification event is emitted asynchronously.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. DATA ARCHITECTURE \(HIGH LEVEL\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Primary durable entities:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `RateLimitRule`: clientId/route pair, requestLimit, windowSeconds, algorithm, active state.) Tj
T*
(- `OTPRecord`: identifier, channel type, hashed OTP, expiry, attempts, used flag.) Tj
T*
(- `Payment`: idempotency key \(unique\), clientId, amount/currency, status, failure reason,) Tj
T*
(timestamps.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
